/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Headlamps give a main (high) beam for empty roads and a dipped (low) beam for traffic.
   - Position lamps (side lamps) mark the car's width at night.
   - Tail lamps are red and come on with the position lamps, typically 5 W each.
   - Interior lamps, the dome, map, vanity, boot and glovebox lamps, are convenience loads.
   - Special-purpose lamps warn or work.
   - The lamp circuit is the same every time: battery → fuse → switch or relay → lamp → earth return (Figure 2.6.1).
   - I is the total current in amperes, ΣP the sum of the lamp powers in watts at their rated voltage and V that voltage in volts.
*/
