/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Levelling is rotation about a horizontal axis (pitch).
   - Swivel, or dynamic bending light, is rotation about a vertical axis (yaw).
   - Many AFS lamps also change the beam pattern with speed: a wide, short town light; the normal country light; a longer, slightly raised motorway light at high speed; and an adverse-weather light that cuts light just ahead of the car, where we
   - The AFS ECU reads the steering angle sensor (wheel angle and rate), the vehicle speed sent over the CAN bus by the ABS ECU from its wheel-speed sensors, front and rear ride-height sensors (the difference gives pitch) and, on newer cars, a f
   - It computes target swivel and pitch angles and commands two small motors per lamp.
   - θ is the pitch angle of the body, Δh the drop of the rear axle in metres with the front axle at its normal height, and b the wheelbase in metres.
   - A matrix headlamp builds the high beam from many LED segments.
*/
